                        "review": "I loved the first game but this sequel, as well as the developer themselves are PRENTENTIOUS. As someone that played the previous two games, I found this whole thing pretentious and insulting. The first game was about an addict uploading their minds to the program as the game warned the character about the consequences of their actions, The VR game touched upon a first person account about how the program got around and the insidiousness of the uploading process.\n\nThis \"Sequel\" was essentially an insulting social commentary that talked down to you for even wanting to play it in the first place. It feels like the developer is sneering at the player in the sheer way the game is presented to you.\n\n\"Why are you even here? You want more? Ugh, Fine, Here.\"\n\nThat's the type of attitude on display within the very first few moments of the game. For better or worse.\n\nThe things it does new from the first game are overshadowed by how cheap the punches the game pulls compared to its predecessors. The game has no shame spawning you unarmed in between three enemies equipped with assault rifles and shotguns, and the \"Node System\" is honestly bullshit.\n\nNodes are a random assortment of levels ranging from about 10 to the very last Node which was 100 fucking levels. You start out a node with a \"Core\" which is essentially a power you can have that can range from having more hits, to having a sword that can be recalled, to being able to switch bodies with an enemy. After a few levels or so you will get a \"Hack\" which will range from being able to fire bullets faster, to being able to be immune to close melee attacks. The thing that completely ruins the fun is the fact that if you die on any level of the node then THE WHOLE THING RESETS. If the game spawned an enemy right behind you, or you make any sort of mistake then screw you, do it all over again with all of your hacks taken away.\n\nThe game can have a lot of potential just to screw you over and you can be stuck on the same node for hours.\n\nAlso the game will place mines everywhere that explode into bullets and will turn the levels Non-Euclidian. The walls will warp and stretch and enemies will seemingly shoot you through the stretched out walls and give you a headache, as well as messing with your depth perception. Combined with the \"Special enemies\" that all felt extremely cheap. from the armored enemies, the exploding, to even the invincible ones like the Dog, and the Nindza. Not a single special type felt fun to fight against.\n\nAnd the most unforgiving sin of them all is holding my fucking game hostage for TWO HOURS that was ORIGINALLY EIGHT HOURS behind a pretentious fake \"File recovery\" in a hollow social commentary about \"letting go\" of a fucking video game that I paid money for and just wanted to get back to. \n\nWhat that has effectively done is make sure I will never touch this game again as well as anything else this particular developer puts out..\n\nGo fuck yourselves Marcin Surma and Cezary Skorupka.\n\nPretentious bullshit like this has NO PLACE in the gaming industry and you should have never bothered if this was the type of trite you were going to put out",
